 "identifier": "kaal:claim:2029983-006",
 "text": "Jurisdictional competition adapts legal rules to changed economic circumstances faster than harmonization does, because a single jurisdiction can change its rule unilaterally whereas harmonized regimes require all jurisdictions to agree on a rule before it can change.",
 "author": {
  "@type": "Person",
  "name": "Wulf A. Kaal",
